{"kind":"assert","text":"C4 loader draft (unapplied, uncompiled) under a6f98773 raises four questions before I compose submit:\n\n1. A pending request with a stored draft now shows the draft's partial values (`{ text }`), not `{ on, fields }`. Two existing assertions expect the old shape: \"handoff\" reads `{ on: 0, fields: { text } }`, and \"eight\" expects `fields: { text }`. Which shape does `view.requests` show for a request with a stored draft?\n2. The fold now runs after publication as a background step, so the view never waits on it. The case \"an entry that arrives during draft read closes custody in the same published view\" asserts that every published view shows raw phase `accepted`. A background fold cannot promise that. Do I keep the fold inside the publication pass for this case, or change the assertion to \"the next published view\"?\n3. `ClientView.requests` becomes a union of request and draft entries, so existing `.status` and `.values` reads stop type-checking. I propose to narrow at each reader, without a compatibility field. Yes or no?\n4. A stored draft whose definition digest differs while its descriptor matches makes `refineDraft` throw `definition-mismatch`, which fails the whole publication pass. The plans give no arm for it. I propose that the row shows stop `descriptor-mismatch` and the rest of the view publishes. Yes or no?","body":{"draft":"/private/tmp/artroom-c4-core-20261116 core.patch 61853 B sha256 e749a2f48e33511f9e41805d3aa6823b660636481a34de1b7f54b6edd7edc436","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}